following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063295/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ff5b367c94cd78e706b851ef08cb499a2e1131773e546cd468cb9ec4b0ff8c7"} {"question" "q-346435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $32$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{u}\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063295/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ff5b367c94cd78e706b851ef08cb499a2e1131773e546cd468cb9ec4b0ff8c7"} {"question" "q-346435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063295/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cde6291e198ceef719653384d387bcbdaa20731b89884afdb61157cac76a2974"} {"question" "q-346435" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" 